      "artist": "Phil Richards from London, UK",
      "credit": "18.06.95 Ballina 169",
      "source": "18.06.95 Ballina 169 (5957581461)",
      "description": "The second batch of locomotives built by General Motors EMD were delivered to Córas Iompair Éireann (CIE) in late 1962. Originally B class, they hung around until 2010. Working both passenger and freights, although as with many of the earlier engines used in Ireland they were not train heat fitted. As such trains would be seen operated with steam generating vans. Services on the branch to Ballina have generally worked as a connection off services between Dublin and Westport either at Claremorris or in more recent years, Manulla Junction. Seen at Ballina on 18 June 1995, 169 has arrived on train A882, 13:00 Manulla Junction to Ballina.",
